{
 "id": "CMP-35",
 "name": "speaker-turntable",
 "version": 1,
 "title": "A product turntable: a speaker turning in 3D",
 "summary": "A bookshelf speaker built from seven primitives (a rounded box, cylinders, tori and flattened spheres) with Scene3D: it turns slowly on a turntable disc and the viewer can drag it round; the server frames it at every angle and window shape, below a title and above a hint.",
 "prompt": "Show our bookshelf speaker as a 3D model that turns slowly on a turntable, with its name above; let people drag it to look at it from any side.",
 "level": 3,
 "family": "CMP",
 "components": [
  "Scene3D"
 ],
 "capabilities": {
  "primary": [
   "3d.scene",
   "3d.mesh"
  ],
  "secondary": [
   "input.drag",
   "time.animation"
  ]
 },
 "use_cases": [
  "onboarding"
 ],
 "form_factor": "phone",
 "keywords": [
  "3d",
  "turntable",
  "product view",
  "product viewer",
  "360 view",
  "rotate product",
  "spin",
  "speaker",
  "loudspeaker",
  "3d model",
  "orbit",
  "drag to rotate",
  "autorotate",
  "showcase"
 ],
 "teaches": [
  "A product from primitives: a box with \"round\" for the cabinet, cylinders and tori with \"axis\": \"z\" for drivers facing the viewer, a flattened sphere (size [x, y, z]) for a dome",
  "autorotate: 20 turns it at 20 degrees a second; orbit (default) still lets a drag take over, and floor: true adds the turntable disc",
  "insetTop / insetBottom keep the overlay's title and hint clear: the scene is framed in what is left and moved below the title",
  "Product colours are document colours with a light and a dark value (resources.colors): the theme's names cover the rest; mono draws every part as a hidden-line wireframe and stops the turn"
 ],
 "pitfalls": [
  "3D support has not landed in androidx yet (coming): this plays in the C++ and TypeScript players only. Don't use it for a screen that must play on Android today",
  "autorotate repaints every frame while the page is shown; for a still product shot leave it 0 and let the drag turn it"
 ],
